{"park":"glacier","fetched":"2026-09-06T06:40:14+00:00","attribution":{"landmarks":"© OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL","summaries":"Wikipedia, CC BY-SA 4.0","boundary":"iNaturalist place 72841"},"landmarks":[{"id":"node/962947477","name":"Beaver Chief Falls","kind":"waterfall","lon":-113.76439,"lat":48.59391,"ele_m":1604.0,"wikidata":"Q85746203","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beaver_Chief_Falls","tour":5,"summary":{"extract":"Beaver Chief Falls is a waterfall located in Glacier National Park, Montana, US. The falls emerge at the top of a hanging valley just beyond the outflow for Lake Ellen Wilson and descend in a series of braided drops a distance of nearly 1,300 feet (400 m), the tallest of which is recorded as being a straight drop of 517 ft (158 m). Below the hanging valley lies Lincoln Lake, where the cascades end. Somewhat inaccessible, the falls require a nearly 20-mile (32 km) round-trip hike to visit.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beaver_Chief_Falls","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","attribution":"Wikipedia"},"photos":[{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Beaver_Chief_Falls_drops_some_1%2C800_feet_from_the_Hanging_Valley_of_Lake_Ellen_Wilson%2C_Glacier_National_Park%2C_Montana%2C_USA._July_22%2C_2007_-_panoramio.jpg/960px-Beaver_Chief_Falls_drops_some_1%2C800_feet_from_the_Hanging_Valley_of_Lake_Ellen_Wilson%2C_Glacier_National_Park%2C_Montana%2C_USA._July_22%2C_2007_-_panoramio.jpg","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Beaver_Chief_Falls_drops_some_1,800_feet_from_the_Hanging_Valley_of_Lake_Ellen_Wilson,_Glacier_National_Park,_Montana,_USA._July_22,_2007_-_panoramio.jpg","dist_m":226,"width":640,"height":480,"license":"CC BY 3.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0","artist":"Gary Miotla"}],"street":null},{"id":"node/963565834","name":"Feather Plume Falls","kind":"waterfall","lon":-113.70289,"lat":48.75107,"ele_m":1955.0,"wikidata":"Q85760698","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Feather_Plume_Falls","tour":4,"summary":{"extract":"Feather Plume Falls is an ephemeral waterfall located above Cataract Creek in Glacier National Park, Montana, US. Feather Plume Falls have several major drops in its 1,500 feet (460 m) from Grinnell Glacier with the highest estimated at 1,080 ft (330 m). The falls are on the northeast slopes of Mount Gould in the Many Glacier region of the park.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Feather_Plume_Falls","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","attribution":"Wikipedia"},"photos":[],"street":null},{"id":"node/963462710","name":"Grinnell Falls","kind":"waterfall","lon":-113.72075,"lat":48.76271,"ele_m":1749.0,"wikidata":"Q85764621","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grinnell_Falls","tour":3,"summary":{"extract":"Grinnell Falls is a waterfall in Glacier National Park, Montana, US. Grinnell Falls have several major drops in its 960 feet (290 m) descent from Grinnell Glacier with the highest estimated at 280 ft (85 m). The falls are in the Many Glacier region of the park, between Mount Grinnell and Angel Wing.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grinnell_Falls","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","attribution":"Wikipedia"},"photos":[{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Bighorn_Sheep%2C_Grinnell_Glacier_Trail_%284120046660%29.jpg/960px-Bighorn_Sheep%2C_Grinnell_Glacier_Trail_%284120046660%29.jpg","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bighorn_Sheep,_Grinnell_Glacier_Trail_(4120046660).jpg","dist_m":301,"width":640,"height":427,"license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","artist":"Greg Willis from Denver, CO, usa"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Grinnell_Falls.jpg/960px-Grinnell_Falls.jpg","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grinnell_Falls.jpg","dist_m":316,"width":640,"height":522,"license":"CC BY 2.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","artist":"Roy Luck"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/View_down_Valley_to_Lake_Sherburne_%284120042712%29.jpg/960px-View_down_Valley_to_Lake_Sherburne_%284120042712%29.jpg","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_down_Valley_to_Lake_Sherburne_(4120042712).jpg","dist_m":317,"width":640,"height":427,"license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","artist":"Greg Willis from Denver, CO, usa"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Lil_Picnic_Buddy_%284120042476%29.jpg/960px-Lil_Picnic_Buddy_%284120042476%29.jpg","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lil_Picnic_Buddy_(4120042476).jpg","dist_m":336,"width":640,"height":427,"license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","artist":"Greg Willis from Denver, CO, usa"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Boat_on_Lake_Josephine_%284119267273%29.jpg/960px-Boat_on_Lake_Josephine_%284119267273%29.jpg","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Boat_on_Lake_Josephine_(4119267273).jpg","dist_m":396,"width":640,"height":427,"license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","artist":"Greg Willis from Denver, CO, usa"}],"street":null},{"id":"node/962207698","name":"Ipasha Falls","kind":"waterfall","lon":-113.80755,"lat":48.8487,"ele_m":1953.0,"wikidata":"Q85769908","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ipasha_Falls","tour":0,"summary":{"extract":"Ipasha Falls is a waterfall located in Glacier National Park, Montana, US. Ipasha Falls descends from Ipasha Glacier to Ipasha Lake and is recorded as having a drop of at least 800 feet (240 m). Located in a remote region north of Many Glacier, the falls can only been seen by a multiday hike on established trails to Mokowanis Lake and then from there along unmaintained trails to Ipasha Lake.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ipasha_Falls","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","attribution":"Wikipedia"},"photos":[],"street":null},{"id